What:		/sys/bus/mipi-dsi/devices/<dsi-device>/mdnie_scenario
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.0
Contact:	omar fityan <me@omarfityan.com>
Description:
		(RW) The scenario the Samsung ANA38407 DDIC's mDNIe
		image-quality engine runs. Reading lists the accepted values
		with the selected one in brackets, e.g. "[ui_auto] hdr_video".

		ui_auto:   stock's start-up UI scenario (UI_APP + AUTO_MODE);
			   the default.
		hdr_video: the HDR-neutral HDR_VIDEO_1 scenario, whose colour
			   remap is the identity; stock selects it while HDR
			   video is on screen.

		A write while the panel is on takes effect immediately; a
		write while it is off is applied at the next panel-on. The
		selection persists across panel power cycles but not across
		a driver reload. It takes effect only while the driver's mdnie
		module parameter is 3 (its default); other values are debug
		overrides.

What:		/sys/bus/mipi-dsi/devices/<dsi-device>/dcs_read
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.0
Contact:	omar fityan <me@omarfityan.com>
Description:
		(RW) Debug read-back of one DDIC register over DSI. Write
		"<register-hex> <length>" (length 1..16) to select; read to
		perform the read, which prints
		"addr[<reg>] len[<n>] : <byte> ...". A read while the panel
		is off fails with -ENODEV; a failed or short transfer fails
		with an error rather than printing a value.

What:		/sys/class/backlight/<dsi-device>/luminance_table
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.0
Contact:	omar fityan <me@omarfityan.com>
Description:
		(RO) Nominal luminance, in cd/m2, of every brightness level
		of the Samsung ANA38407 panel's backlight, from 0 to
		max_brightness: max_brightness + 1 unsigned decimal integers,
		space-separated, in level order, newline-terminated. The
		values are the vendor's panel data file figures rounded to
		whole cd/m2 (its NORMAL_CANDELA_MAP below hbm_threshold, its
		HBM_CANDELA_MAP from hbm_threshold up), not measurements of
		the individual unit. It is one table describing one property,
		published whole so that a reader gets a consistent copy in a
		single read. It is a constant of the panel and never changes.

What:		/sys/class/backlight/<dsi-device>/hbm_threshold
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.0
Contact:	omar fityan <me@omarfityan.com>
Description:
		(RO) The first brightness level served in the panel's
		high-brightness mode, as an unsigned decimal integer. Levels
		from it up to max_brightness drive the DDIC's high-brightness
		state; luminance stays continuous across the boundary (see
		luminance_table). A constant of the panel.
